==============================================================================
PATCH-SHAPE ROBUSTNESS of N_cross (smallest N with U>3N, best radius)
==============================================================================
            form   D*  dens   disk    box   eucl
  triangular(-3)    7     6     43     49     43
      square(-4)    5     4    101    169    101
         disc-12   28     6     79    121     79
     disc-15(d5)   16     5     71     81     71
          disc-7   16     5     97    121     97
  disc-15(2,1,2)   32     6     83     81     83

  minimizer under  disk patch: triangular(-3) at N=43
  minimizer under   box patch: triangular(-3) at N=49
  minimizer under  eucl patch: triangular(-3) at N=43

Note: for a binary quadratic form Q, Q(i,j) IS the squared Euclidean length of
the embedded lattice vector, so the 'eucl' round disk == the 'disk' Q-ball
(they should agree exactly). The 'box' patch is the genuinely different shape.
